GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:33856:     "outcome_note": "PASS 4 (self-declared claude-fable-5-1; a claim). RATIFY on an ANALYTIC sweep (108 cells + read-side + helper edits; no mutant built -- stated as a reading). Measured only coherence: 96 emitted rows == 96 gate names, 0 missing, 0 extra, no name over 15 chars, one $PCC2LOG. Every E/UNREACHABLE/C warrant re-derived true from source (SCCERR stores 0 only; odd read cells alignment-fault / NO_EXCEPTIONS dispatch; d->warned written only in the helper). PRETABLE split judged honest with the mtimes. Nit: 'five dcl rows count generic text' is mechanically seven rows, five ARMS unpinned -- corrected. ITS RATIFY DID NOT CONSIDER the helper SET-line edits (|= -> =, (1u<<bit) -> 1) that four seats derived, nor len 8 -- OVERTURNED provisionally; part 4 measures them. Count arguments, not seats: the escapes carry derivations, the ratify carries a sweep that omitted them.",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:33857:     "note": "PASS 4 (self-declared claude-fable-5-1; a claim). RATIFY on an ANALYTIC sweep (108 cells + read-side + helper edits; no mutant built -- stated as a reading). Measured only coherence: 96 emitted rows == 96 gate names, 0 missing, 0 extra, no name over 15 chars, one $PCC2LOG. Every E/UNREACHABLE/C warrant re-derived true from source (SCCERR stores 0 only; odd read cells alignment-fault / NO_EXCEPTIONS dispatch; d->warned written only in the helper). PRETABLE split judged honest with the mtimes. Nit: 'five dcl rows count generic text' is mechanically seven rows, five ARMS unpinned -- corrected. ITS RATIFY DID NOT CONSIDER the helper SET-line edits (|= -> =, (1u<<bit) -> 1) that four seats derived, nor len 8 -- OVERTURNED provisionally; part 4 measures them. Count arguments, not seats: the escapes carry derivations, the ratify carries a sweep that omitted them."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:33868:     "outcome_note": "PASS 4 READER (fresh seat). BUILT and MEASURED on the shipped 96-row instrument (frozen md5 72759b4f, own clone, BASE re-scored 96/96): M_LATCHASSIGN (d->warned |= -> =, ONE character) 96/96 TOTAL SWEEP with the mutation proven (0 x '|=', 1 x 'd->warned = ') and the binary newer; M_BITSHIFT (1u<<bit -> 1u<<(bit+1)) 96/96 and EQUIVALENT (bit identity has no consumer) -- the clause-(f) control. The grid enumerated twelve call sites and not the helper's own predicate: the fix introduced THIRTEEN predicates. Also: len 8 (put d via store_64bit_word, re-derived) is coverage debt the pass-3 codex seat had already named and pass 4 dropped -- the rewritten-row-list class; fatal->debug severity unobservable by text rows (disclosure owed); break -> return 0 (the FAULT member) unmeasured; the SCCERR E deriver keyed on a correlate (the writer is addressed by relative_addr) -- corrected to grep pcctwo_reg[; THREE instruments (3dcf73de/280d9ab3/72759b4f) presented as one -- the transfer is sound (only rb t1ctl's want strings and acc all's session differ) and is now stated; 'adding rows cannot un-kill' is the wrong warrant for a REWRITTEN row -- corrected; PRETABLE_amendments.out re-created the mtime defect by holding Sections 5-7 -- one file per amendment from now; the proof lines printed before the score read as the previous mutant's -- now prefixed with the mutant's name. All 28 S cells walked against the arm masks and hold; E and UNREACHABLE re-derived true from source. ACCEPTED IN FULL; measured in part 4: latch aba, latch same2, latch all d, acc pscale ign, acc ipl ro; mutants M_LEN8_VECBASE, M_LATCH_ASSIGN, M_LATCH_BIT0, M_GROW_IPL, M_RET0_GENCTL.",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:33869:     "note": "PASS 4 READER (fresh seat). BUILT and MEASURED on the shipped 96-row instrument (frozen md5 72759b4f, own clone, BASE re-scored 96/96): M_LATCHASSIGN (d->warned |= -> =, ONE character) 96/96 TOTAL SWEEP with the mutation proven (0 x '|=', 1 x 'd->warned = ') and the binary newer; M_BITSHIFT (1u<<bit -> 1u<<(bit+1)) 96/96 and EQUIVALENT (bit identity has no consumer) -- the clause-(f) control. The grid enumerated twelve call sites and not the helper's own predicate: the fix introduced THIRTEEN predicates. Also: len 8 (put d via store_64bit_word, re-derived) is coverage debt the pass-3 codex seat had already named and pass 4 dropped -- the rewritten-row-list class; fatal->debug severity unobservable by text rows (disclosure owed); break -> return 0 (the FAULT member) unmeasured; the SCCERR E deriver keyed on a correlate (the writer is addressed by relative_addr) -- corrected to grep pcctwo_reg[; THREE instruments (3dcf73de/280d9ab3/72759b4f) presented as one -- the transfer is sound (only rb t1ctl's want strings and acc all's session differ) and is now stated; 'adding rows cannot un-kill' is the wrong warrant for a REWRITTEN row -- corrected; PRETABLE_amendments.out re-created the mtime defect by holding Sections 5-7 -- one file per amendment from now; the proof lines printed before the score read as the previous mutant's -- now prefixed with the mutant's name. All 28 S cells walked against the arm masks and hold; E and UNREACHABLE re-derived true from source. ACCEPTED IN FULL; measured in part 4: latch aba, latch same2, latch all d, acc pscale ign, acc ipl ro; mutants M_LEN8_VECBASE, M_LATCH_ASSIGN, M_LATCH_BIT0, M_GROW_IPL, M_RET0_GENCTL."
