GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:45137:     "note": "Measuring seat, clone /tmp/gxopus529close restored and deleted; 15 runs of the frozen 85-row test, all matching its written PRETABLE.  Spot-checks lt_len 84/85, c_dog 83/85 detected.  ELEVEN non-equivalent 85/85 survivors, each shown real by a discriminator: hi_gate (decline gated on HARDINT, a field the tail reads -- floor), pa_gate, rearm4, pre4, rearm_time, ctl_collide, wst_mc2, rd_hi, lt_blk, wnz_lbl, acc4_210.  TIME s1 66-990 across 52 cells vs 6.6e6.  Corrected the TIME comment's mechanism (the first tick fires right after the first ld).  Fix: no defect."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:45218:     "note": "Measuring seat, clones /tmp/gxopus529c2 (+ a batch-3 clone) restored cmp-clean and deleted; predictions written before each build (PRETABLE2.out, PRETABLE3.out).  On the 111-row test: istat_leak (a refused read at INTSTAT answering the register) 111/111, dog_leak 111/111, istat_lane 111/111, rd_hi_lh 111/111 -- each shown NON-equivalent by a guest-only discriminator (0x0 vs 0xff..ff / ..ffef / 0x708); controls rd_hi_lb 110, rd_lh_all 106, soft_gate 93.  On the main loop's 121-row repair (BIT 0x10000001): istat_leak caught 119/121, but the BYTE-LANE form `odata = reg >> (8*(8-len-(relative_addr&7)))' at INTSTAT still 121/121 -- the seed was nonzero only in the low byte and a label's refused read names bytes 0-1.  Also: imask lb/lh v0, dog v0, ctl v0 were reddened by 0 of 47 table-4 runs (every table-4 answer mutant was the odata=1 constant); POSTTABLE 4's denominator counted those cells.  ADOPTED: repair 7 (seed 0x0101000010000001: nonzero in bytes 0, 1 and 7); lane-form leaks at REV/CONTROL/TIME disclosed EQUIVALENT (their top lanes are always 0 in the model).  Fix: no defect."
