GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:45719:     "note": "[NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: MEASURED from the subagent transcript (per-message `model' and `stop_reason'; _scratchpad/agent_models.py), the answer this entry credits to fable5 was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 at 19:50:12Z (agent a06935485cd6d5125) -- claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason \"refusal\" at 2026-09-16T19:35:00Z and the Agent tool re-ran the rest on opus-4-8, keeping the seat's identity line.  Kept as an opus-4-8 READING, not a fable5 answer; the file carries a dated provenance note since 2026-09-26; the first-hand ruling is regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md (the first-hand fable5 ruling of 2026-09-25, entered below; it re-anchors C3, D7, Q3 and STOP). ***  ADJUDICATION, firing LAST, on 9 of 9 mandated seats plus kimi-k3:cloud -- NOT provisional.  *** IT OVERTURNED TWO OF ITS OWN PRIOR RULINGS AND UPHELD BOTH DISPOSITIONS I HAD FLAGGED AS SUSPECT, which is the be-harder-on-the-ruling-in-your-favour rule doing exactly what it exists to do: asked which of my dispositions was wrong, it answered `none of the ones you flagged -- the wrong ones are mine'. ***  PART A VERDICT **REPAIR 13** -- closing pass 7 does NOT close; the K-class is a floor breach.  **D7 RULED FLOOR, overturning its own RA3**, on four independent grounds, the first in the diff itself: the fix's own decline arm READS d->warned at dev_sgi_ip32.c:314, in a hunk THIS DIFF ADDS, so the latch is a device-state lvalue the fix's repair path reads -- a floor axis by the pass-11 definition and the M_ICLR precedent, and by the round's own practice (it built and measured the shrink).  Bounded, not #392: the floor is the diff-closed 56-cell product.  **Q1, the units: the FLOOR is the 23 open guest-visible cells (31 minus the 8 already pinned), NOT all 28 latch-SET mutants and NOT all 56 product cells** -- a mutant at an equivalent or pinned cell teaches nothing, a row at a cell no mutant reaches is unfalsifiable, so the floor is the INTERSECTION.  PRETABLE 11 carries the WHOLE product with per-cell disposition: 23 rowed, 8 already-pinned, 10 equivalent (no row), 5 host-diagnostic (clause-(e), disclosed with F1/F1b/F3's measurements); 10+5+8+23 = 46.  Q3: table 11 AND closing pass 8, BOTH -- retyped rows are measured not assumed, and pass 8 VERIFIES the enumeration cell-by-cell and must close on a zero carried WITH its denominator.  D1's grade was under-determined while D7 was punted and is now SECURED by it.  D3/D4 (the two disclosures I flagged) UPHELD, each verified against the seat's measurements and each with an independent second reason.  L4 it names: its own RA3, and the header's `46 kinds' vs `46 ENTRIES, not 46 kinds' inconsistency (grok's nit, confirmed) -- both corrected in place."
