F2 VERDICT: RATIFY WITH CHANGES (5)

The one-line deletion stands; I find no open detector-floor cell. I checked the source at `987cb596`, parsed the repaired mutator, and reconciled all eleven raw logs. This verdict addresses the supplied packet; later scratch drafts already incorporate some corrections below.

| Item | Disposition and reason |
|---|---|
| P1 | **UPHOLD** — the preserved mutator now parses and matches the scratch copy; the failed application remains documented. |
| P2 | **UPHOLD** — the revised destination disclosure accurately distinguishes FPUL observation from DRn observation. |
| P3 | **REFINE** — disclose unobserved outputs as well as unvaried inputs; also distinguish legal untested states from reserved combinations. |
| P4 | **UPHOLD** — `0x7fc00000` is signaling under the cited SH-4 convention; retaining the oracle is correct. |
| P5 | **UPHOLD** — the arithmetic reconciles: 25 two-mode vectors plus two single-mode vectors give 52 sessions; nine discriminate. |
