**P10 is the accepted disposition most clearly wrong as written.** The cited pseudocode says `undefined_operation()` for a reserved combination. That does not establish the specific exception the emulator must raise. The architectural description likewise calls unsupported precision-mode results undefined. FSRRA supplies a fork policy precedent, not proof of the other instructions’ architectural exception contract. Keep this as a policy/specification investigation unless stronger evidence establishes a required result. [SH-4 architecture specification, FPSCR description](https://www.st.com/resource/en/user_manual/um0341-sh4-32bit-cpu-core-architecture---stmicroelectronics.pdf)

The five changes I count are these independent arguments:

1. **Correct P10’s specification claim and class scope.** Replace the asserted exception oracle with the unresolved policy question above. The cited manual’s explicit `undefined_operation()` sites also include **FMAC, FRCHG and FSCHG**; the four-instruction filing is incomplete. This does not require changing those handlers in #576.

2. **Narrow P6’s historical claim.** The [17:15 plan](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:26) describes all eight destinations as DR2. Its `M_g` prediction belongs to that instrument; `M_f` is conditional, and `M_d` and `M_gm` are absent. It demonstrates advance planning, but cannot certify the final instrument’s complete predictions or the original PRETABLE’s write order. The later draft’s qualified account is substantially better.

3. **Correct the instrument-preservation statement.** The change was not exclusively comments: `ftrcS-nan qNaN+` became `sNaN+`, changing a string literal and emitted output. My AST comparison finds exactly that executable-tree difference; normalizing the label makes the complete ASTs equal. Furthermore, [ASRUN_NOTE.txt](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/killtable_20261102/ASRUN_NOTE.txt) correctly identifies the as-run file as a **reconstruction**, not an original preserved at execution time. Use that precise account. Neither fact invalidates the scores.

4. **Reduce P11’s binary-identity claim to the evidence retained.** [run_probe_leg.sh](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/killtable_20261102/run_probe_leg.sh) records `md5sum … | cut -c1-12`. Matching size and 12 hexadecimal characters strongly support identity, but do not document a byte comparison or even matching full digests. Say “matching recorded fingerprints.” Clause (b) remains supported by the reinstatement and measured failures.

5. **Disclose the missing output observations.** This is the additional coverage gap: varying FPSCR inputs and observing FPSCR outputs are different obligations. Appending
   
   ```c
   cpu->cd.sh.fpscr |= 4;  /* spuriously set the inexact flag */
   ```
   
   after the fixed handler’s DRn stores would escape all 52 checks **by inspection; I did not build it**. The probe never reads FPSCR afterward, and the readback instructions do not depend on that flag. Disclose this under clause (e), without adding rows. Also qualify “writes DRn only” as the **data-register destination** claim: the architectural instruction has FPSCR exception effects, which this fix does not implement or validate.

The owner’s Astra requirement and the listed application, propagation, rebuild and gate checks remain prerequisites to landing. No files were changed during this review.

